```text
ORDINANCE NO. ________

ENTITLED: "AN ORDINANCE APPROVING AND ESTABLISHING REVISED
WATER AND SEWER RATES, TAP AND SYSTEM DEVELOPMENT
FEES,
ADMINISTRATIVE
FEES,
SERVICE
CHARGES
AND
PENALTIES, AND SEPTIC AND COMMERCIAL WASTE DUMP RATES,
AS RECOMMENDED BY THE BOARD OF PUBLIC UTILITIES."

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:

Section 1.  That, pursuant to Wyoming Statute §15-7-407, the Board of Public Utilities
("BOARD") shall fix the rates for water and sanitary sewer services furnished to customers, and
any revision thereof is subject to the governing body's review, modification and approval.

Section 2.  That the BOARD is authorized by Wyoming statute and the Cheynne municipal
code to fix rates, fees and penalties for water and sanitary sewer services furnished to customers
to:
A. Pay interest charges and principal payments on all outstanding water and sanitary
sewer loans and bonds as they are due;
B. Pay for the operation and maintenance of the water and sanitary sewer systems,
including salaries, wages and benefits, and the cost of all materials and supplies
necessary for repairs, replacements and upgrades to the systems;
C. Cover all miscellaneous expenses;
D. Cover all usual extensions and enlargements, together with a reasonable allowance for
emergency and unforeseen expenses; and
E. Provide and maintain a depreciation fund for each of the water and sanitary sewer
departments.

Section 3.  That the BOARD has determined that an increase in the water and sanitary
sewer rates is justified to ensure adequate revenue is generated in order to pay for costs associated
with those services rendered.

Section 4.  That, pursuant to Section 13.04.140 of the municipal code, the BOARD must
establish rates and charges for the consumption of city utility services, charges and fees for
connections, inspections, penalties, shutoff penalties and meter installations. Such rates, charges,
fees and penalties must thereafter be approved by the Governing Body and filed with the City
Clerk and business office of the BOARD.

Section 5.  That, in accordance with City Ordinance 4505, adopted on June 12, 2023, prior
to the beginning of each fiscal year the BOARD is required to calculate new rates for water and
sewer services based on the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price Index, All Urban
Consumers, Water and Sewer Maintenance and the Wyoming Cost of Living Index – Southeast
Region, and prepare new rate schedules for water and sewer services.

11:49 am, Apr 23, 2024
```

### Page 2 of 20

```text
Section 6.  That the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price Index, All Urban
Consumers, Water and Sewer Maintenance for the calendar year 2023 was 4.7% and the Wyoming
Cost of Living Index – Southeast Region for the second quarter of 2023 was 4.3%; and the
Engineering News Record Construction Cost Index (ENR CCI) for calendar year 2023 was 4.2%.

Section 7.  That by Resolution No. 2024-01, adopted April 29, 2024, the BOARD
established revised water rates to be charged to customers of the Cheyenne Water System as shown
and set forth on the resolution attached hereto as Exhibit A.

Section 8.  That by Resolution No. 2024-02, adopted April 29, 2024, the BOARD
established revised sewer rates to be charged to customers of the Cheyenne Sewer System as
shown and set forth on the resolution attached hereto as Exhibit B.

Section 9.  That by Resolution No. 2024-03, adopted April 29, 2024, the BOARD
established revised Water and Sewer Connections Fees, System Development Fees and other
related fees as shown and set forth on the resolution attached hereto as Exhibit C.

Section 10.  That by Resolution No. 2024-04, adopted April 29, 2024, the BOARD
established revised Administrative fees, and Service Charges and Penalties, as shown and set forth
on the resolution attached hereto as Exhibit D.

Section 11.  That by Resolution No. 2024-05, adopted April 29, 2024, the BOARD
established revised Septic Waste Dump and Commercial Waste Rates to be charged to the
customers of the Cheyenne Water and Sewer Systems as shown and set forth on the resolution
attached hereto as Exhibit E.

Section 12.  That the Governing Body has reviewed the rates, charges penalties and fees
established by the BOARD for water and sewer services and hereby approves the water and sewer
rate schedules attached hereto.

Section 13.  That, prior to the beginning of each fiscal year, the BOARD shall calculate
new rates for Water and Sewer services based on the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price
Index, All Urban Consumers, Water and Sewer Maintenance, Wyoming Cost of Living Index –
Southeast Region, and the Engineering News Record Construction Cost Index (ENR CCI), and
prepare new rate schedules for Water and Sewer Services that shall be presented, in the form of an
ordinance, to the Governing Body.

Section 14.  This ordinance shall be in full force and effect upon approval and publication.

